# 11. CRITICAL BUSINESS LOGIC

These rules are mandatory.

RULE 1 — PRIVACY

Students can only access their own marks and report cards.

RULE 2 — CLASS VALIDATION

Enrollment numbers must exist in the HOD-uploaded class roster before enrollment approval.

RULE 3 — PROFESSOR PERMISSIONS

A professor can only modify subjects assigned to them and authorized by the HOD.

RULE 4 — MARKS VALIDATION

Obtained marks must be between zero and the configured maximum marks.

RULE 5 — LOCKING

A locked subject cannot be edited through normal professor operations.

RULE 6 — SYNCHRONIZED PUBLICATION

No student can access partial subject results.

All required subject submissions must be locked before publication.

RULE 7 — ATOMIC RESULT RELEASE

Publication must be a single database transaction.

RULE 8 — AUDITABILITY

Every marks change and administrative correction must be traceable.

RULE 9 — HISTORICAL RECORDS

Published historical results must remain accessible and must not be silently overwritten.

RULE 10 — AUTHORIZATION

Every sensitive operation must be validated by the backend, not merely hidden in the UI.

